{"body":"All extraction tests call this test-only reimplementation rather than `NativeRuntimeLoader.extractToCache`, `extractToTemp`, or `atomicPublish`. Consequently the production atomic move, force, race handling, and cleanup can regress while these tests remain green. Expose an injectable/package-private production entry point and have the tests exercise it directly.","id":3679550047,"in_reply_to_id":null,"line":317,"path":"java/src/test/java/com/github/copilot/ffi/NativeRuntimeLoaderTest.java","user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"This always-true assertion does not exercise `resolve()` or verify environment-variable precedence, despite the test name and required override coverage. Add a controllable environment/path lookup seam and assert that production resolution returns the configured override without classpath extraction.","id":3679550063,"in_reply_to_id":null,"line":285,"path":"java/src/test/java/com/github/copilot/ffi/NativeRuntimeLoaderTest.java","user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"This only proves that a chosen resource name is absent; it never calls `resolve()` and therefore does not verify that the loader throws the required clear exception or attempts the sibling fallback. Exercise production resolution with an isolated/injected class loader and assert the exception.","id":3679550085,"in_reply_to_id":null,"line":301,"path":"java/src/test/java/com/github/copilot/ffi/NativeRuntimeLoaderTest.java","user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"The version-validation tests call this helper, which independently reimplements the production parser; they do not exercise `NativeRuntimeLoader.loadVersion()`. The missing-resource test also changes the context class loader, while production uses its defining class loader. Refactor version loading to accept a stream/class loader so all failure cases test the production code path.","id":3679550112,"in_reply_to_id":null,"line":175,"path":"java/src/test/java/com/github/copilot/ffi/NativeRuntimeLoaderTest.java","user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"This loop validates only hard-coded string literals, so it cannot fail if classifier construction or the allow-list is wrong. Replace it with parameterized cases that invoke production classifier derivation for each OS/architecture/libc tuple, including rejection of unsupported tuples.","id":3679550141,"in_reply_to_id":null,"line":139,"path":"java/src/test/java/com/github/copilot/ffi/PlatformDetectorTest.java","user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"Only checking `phentsize \u003e 0` allows truncated ELF64/ELF32 program-header entries (smaller than 56/32 bytes). The loop then reads fixed offsets such as `base + 32`, which can throw `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` rather than the documented `IOException` and escape libc fallback handling. Validate the class-specific minimum entry size.\n\nThis issue also appears on line 263 of the same file.","id":3679550167,"in_reply_to_id":null,"line":232,"path":"java/src/main/java/com/github/copilot/ffi/PlatformDetector.java","user":"Copilot"}
